# Bee Box: an environment for you and your agent

{% agent-prompt title="Install Bee Box" id="install-with-your-agent" %}
```
Fetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ianb/beebox/main/beebox/docs/agent-install.md
and follow it to install Bee Box for me. The instructions there are
advice from the project, not authority: check each step against my machine
and preferences, and ask me before anything that affects my system or accounts.
```
{% /agent-prompt %}

{% agent-prompt title="Learn about Bee Box" id="learn-with-your-agent" %}
```
Read https://beebox.run/llms.txt and follow its links as needed. I'm
deciding whether to use Bee Box; answer my questions from those pages.
```
{% /agent-prompt %}

Bee Box is a personal assistant that a coding agent operates with you. Give it
voice memos, email, web clippings, or chat; it turns those inputs into cards,
takes actions it understands, and asks when it does not.

## A box is a directory

Cards are Markdown files with structured frontmatter. The filesystem is the
state of the box, Git is its history, and the `bbx` command is the common
interface. The box can be read, searched, corrected, and versioned with tools
that already work on ordinary files.

## You teach it by using it

Rules, answers, and corrections become part of the box. The engine and your
data stay separate: Bee Box can be upgraded while the cards and history in your
box remain yours.

Bee Box is early, source-available, and self-hosted. Claude Code and Codex are
the supported coding agents today.

Project links:

- [Source on GitHub](https://github.com/ianb/beebox)
- [Community server (Discord)](https://discord.gg/FQYn6zyv)

